Feature: Masking of Invoice Numbers in d_product_revenue_clone Table

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog "purgo_databricks" is accessible
    And the Unity Catalog Schema "purgo_playground" is selected
    And the table "d_product_revenue_clone" does not exist
    When the table "d_product_revenue" is cloned to "d_product_revenue_clone"

  Scenario: Successfully mask the last four digits of invoice_number
    Given the "d_product_revenue_clone" table exists with column "invoice_number" as bigint
    When the PySpark masking logic is executed to replace the last four digits of "invoice_number" with "*"
    Then the "invoice_number" column in "d_product_revenue_clone" should have the last four digits masked
    And the masked "invoice_number" should be stored as a string

  Scenario Outline: Masking various invoice_number formats
    Given the "d_product_revenue_clone" table contains a record with "invoice_number" <invoice_number>
    When the PySpark masking logic is executed
    Then the "invoice_number" should be masked as <masked_invoice_number>

    Examples:
      | invoice_number | masked_invoice_number |
      | 1234567890     | 123456****            |
      | 987654321       | 98765****             |
      | 1000           | ****                   |
      | 56789          | 5****                  |

  Scenario: Handle non-numeric invoice_number values
    Given the "d_product_revenue_clone" table contains a record with "invoice_number" as a non-numeric string "INV12345"
    When the PySpark masking logic is executed
    Then an error "Invalid invoice_number format for masking" should be raised

  Scenario: Ensure data type consistency after masking
    Given the "d_product_revenue_clone" table has "invoice_number" as bigint
    When the PySpark masking logic converts "invoice_number" to string for masking
    Then the "invoice_number" column should be of type string after masking

  Scenario: Failure to drop existing clone table
    Given the table "d_product_revenue_clone" exists and cannot be dropped
    When attempting to drop the existing "d_product_revenue_clone" table
    Then an error "Failed to drop existing d_product_revenue_clone table" should be thrown

  Scenario: Missing invoice_number column in clone table
    Given the table "d_product_revenue_clone" does not contain the "invoice_number" column
    When the PySpark masking logic is executed
    Then an error "invoice_number column is missing in d_product_revenue_clone table" should be raised
